WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:02.371
[Conan] While I was in Haiti I visited the

00:00:02.371 --> 00:00:04.004
Ecole Nouvelle Zoranje.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.412
A school that serves some
of the poorest children

00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:08.226
living in Port-au-Prince.

00:00:08.226 --> 00:00:11.226
(children chanting)

00:00:15.508 --> 00:00:17.349
(group chanting)

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:20.099
(group chanting)

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:25.667
(children chanting)

00:00:27.577 --> 00:00:29.827
(chanting)

00:00:33.871 --> 00:00:36.778
I hear a lot of giggling,
is that a good sign?

00:00:36.778 --> 00:00:38.447
Am I pretty? Est-ce belle?

00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:39.836
[Children] Oui!

00:00:39.836 --> 00:00:41.067
Ah, Est-ce belle, eh?

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:43.274
[Children] Oui!

00:00:43.274 --> 00:00:45.949
(children chattering)

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:48.199
(laughter)

00:00:55.122 --> 00:00:58.039
(children singing)

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:05.032
I'm okay!

00:01:05.032 --> 00:01:06.303
(children screeching)

00:01:06.303 --> 00:01:07.653
I'm good again!

00:01:07.653 --> 00:01:08.486
[Children] Oui!

00:01:08.486 --> 00:01:09.319
Bonjou!

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:10.247
[Children] Bonjou!

00:01:10.247 --> 00:01:11.729
Hi, don't mind me.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:12.695
I'm just gonna join you,

00:01:12.695 --> 00:01:13.562
just don't mind me,

00:01:13.562 --> 00:01:14.673
I'm good.

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:15.506
Hi, hi,

00:01:15.506 --> 00:01:19.006
I'm gonna need a little more room up here.

00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:30.759
Kinda sticks up a little bit.

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:31.592
Hi.

00:01:35.441 --> 00:01:37.358
Eyes forward, up there.

00:01:39.377 --> 00:01:42.877
(children read in unison)

00:01:50.889 --> 00:01:54.389
(children read in unison)

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.433
Can I try?

00:02:00.433 --> 00:02:01.483
Can I try?

00:02:01.483 --> 00:02:02.418
(clears throat)

00:02:02.418 --> 00:02:03.251
Noo say

00:02:03.251 --> 00:02:04.743
I seeyen

00:02:04.743 --> 00:02:05.959
no kway

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.667
non te noo,

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:08.500
noo...

00:02:10.171 --> 00:02:11.004
Noo Sa

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.802
koo nu ya see yo

00:02:14.802 --> 00:02:16.135
respecte Nooooo!

00:02:16.997 --> 00:02:19.247
(cheering)

00:02:20.283 --> 00:02:22.630
(chanting)

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.880
(drumming)

00:02:33.829 --> 00:02:36.829
(children laughing)

00:02:38.609 --> 00:02:40.859
(drumming)

00:02:46.462 --> 00:02:47.295
Yah!

00:02:50.037 --> 00:02:52.018
(children laughing)

00:02:52.018 --> 00:02:52.851
Yes!

00:02:52.851 --> 00:02:53.684
She gets me!

00:02:53.684 --> 00:02:55.138
(audience clapping)

00:02:55.138 --> 00:02:57.339
Finally someone gets me.

00:02:57.339 --> 00:03:00.256
(children singing)

00:03:20.122 --> 00:03:23.122
(children laughing)

00:03:24.785 --> 00:03:26.075
Oh thank you!

00:03:26.075 --> 00:03:26.908
Merci!

00:03:27.845 --> 00:03:30.928
(classroom chanting)

00:03:31.793 --> 00:03:34.043
(drumming)

00:03:51.761 --> 00:03:53.219
Finit!

00:03:53.219 --> 00:03:54.052
Yeah!

00:03:54.052 --> 00:03:55.590
As I was leaving the school,

00:03:55.590 --> 00:04:00.059
I was suddenly surrounded by
my very curious classmates.

00:04:00.059 --> 00:04:01.732
Who's the--What did she ask?

00:04:01.732 --> 00:04:03.222
[Interpreter] She ask you who is the

00:04:03.222 --> 00:04:04.159
President of the United States.

00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:05.150
Who is the President of
the United States now?

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:05.984
[Interpreter] Yes.

00:04:05.984 --> 00:04:08.309
Oh. Okay. This is awkward.

00:04:08.309 --> 00:04:09.895
His name is Donald Trump.

00:04:09.895 --> 00:04:12.630
Who's heard of Donald Trump?

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.688
Can you translate Donald
Trump was on television,

00:04:14.688 --> 00:04:16.179
(interpreter translates)

00:04:16.179 --> 00:04:17.691
and then a bunch of grown ups got drunk

00:04:17.691 --> 00:04:19.718
(interpreter translates)

00:04:19.718 --> 00:04:20.913
and they made him president.

00:04:20.913 --> 00:04:23.025
(audience laughter)

00:04:23.025 --> 00:04:27.046
And this man, this crazy
man with crazy hair,

00:04:27.046 --> 00:04:29.670
he became president, that's
why I'm moving to Haiti.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:30.503
My wife says I'm crazy.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.667
Do you think that she's right?

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.662
(interpreter translates)

00:04:34.662 --> 00:04:36.058
[Children] No!

00:04:36.058 --> 00:04:37.158
You don't think I'm crazy?

00:04:37.158 --> 00:04:37.991
(interpreter translates)

00:04:37.991 --> 00:04:39.324
[Children] No!

00:04:41.553 --> 00:04:43.136
Ask the president the same question--

00:04:43.136 --> 00:04:45.386
(laughter)

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.694
[Interpreter] He ask what
did Trump say about Haiti.

00:04:48.694 --> 00:04:50.721
Uh Trump, what did Trump say about Haiti?

00:04:50.721 --> 00:04:51.554
Yeah

00:04:51.554 --> 00:04:52.762
Oh boy, I'm not gonna--

00:04:52.762 --> 00:04:54.209
I'm not gonna--

00:04:54.209 --> 00:04:55.718
What'd you say?

00:04:55.718 --> 00:04:56.968
What'd she say?

00:04:57.831 --> 00:04:58.973
She said don't pay him no mind.

00:04:58.973 --> 00:05:00.646
(laughter)

00:05:00.646 --> 00:05:03.249
She's like don't worry about him--

00:05:03.249 --> 00:05:04.614
What do you know that we don't know?

00:05:04.614 --> 00:05:07.313
These kids are fascinated
with my freckles, aren't they.

00:05:07.313 --> 00:05:09.478
Ask them if they've seen freckles before.

00:05:09.478 --> 00:05:11.728
(interpreter translates)

00:05:11.728 --> 00:05:12.751
[Children] No.

00:05:12.751 --> 00:05:13.670
Do you like them?

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.439
[Children] Oui.

00:05:15.439 --> 00:05:17.113
The freckles don't come off by the way.

00:05:17.113 --> 00:05:18.196
They stay on.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:35.217
Maybe Americans need to
help Haiti put things back,

00:05:35.217 --> 00:05:36.384
is that right?

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:49.998
I'm not gonna take your stuff.

00:05:49.998 --> 00:05:52.498
I'm not gonna take your stuff.

00:05:56.773 --> 00:05:58.101
(interpeter laughs)

00:05:58.101 --> 00:05:58.942
Can I say something?

00:05:58.942 --> 00:06:02.510
I think you have--this
is your next president.

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.774
She is the president, she is
the next president of Haiti,

00:06:04.774 --> 00:06:05.815
right here.

00:06:05.815 --> 00:06:08.401
No, she is not wrong that,

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:11.983
that America in history
has not been good to Haiti.

00:06:11.983 --> 00:06:14.671
But there's still a chance
for America to be better

00:06:14.671 --> 00:06:16.491
to Haiti, I think.

00:06:16.491 --> 00:06:19.028
There's still a chance.

00:06:19.028 --> 00:06:20.488
Does that sound good to you?

00:06:20.488 --> 00:06:21.604
[Interpreter] Now you're talkin, bro.

00:06:21.604 --> 00:06:22.637
Oh good, so you agree with me.

00:06:22.637 --> 00:06:25.379
We'll make a deal on that?

00:06:25.379 --> 00:06:26.462
A deal? Okay?

00:06:29.982 --> 00:06:31.620
[Interpreter] She wants to be the

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.846
President of the United States of America.

00:06:32.846 --> 00:06:34.873
Alright, ask her if she
can do it starting now.

00:06:34.873 --> 00:06:37.389
(interpreter translates)

00:06:37.389 --> 00:06:39.297
Yes! Just ask her if she tweets.

00:06:39.297 --> 00:06:40.421
Does she tweet?

00:06:40.421 --> 00:06:43.492
(interpreter translates)

00:06:43.492 --> 00:06:44.835
Perfect. Perfect.

00:06:44.835 --> 00:06:45.668
She doesn't do tweets.

00:06:45.668 --> 00:06:46.501
Perfect.

